Subject: [PATCH] src: code6cac_c2 / config declarations of func_8004153C and
 D_800A3708 reconciled (owner ruling Q65, step 6)

code6cac_c2.c and config.c (one original file, owner ruling Q65) declare two symbols differently; each gets
its one truthful type before the merge. Byte-identical (full build SHA1 == oracle, every object compared).
Generator and evidence: memory/grind/q65-adoption/q56/adopt/s06_apply.py.

- func_8004153C (defined in text1a_post.c as `s32 func_8004153C(s32 a0)`; returns a record pointer):
  code6cac_c2 declared `extern s32 *func_8004153C(s32);` (calls with one argument), config declared
  `extern void *func_8004153C(void);` (calls `func_8004153C()`). One declaration serves both call forms only
  unprototyped: `extern s32 *func_8004153C();` in both files (the argument is an s32 either way, so default
  promotion changes nothing; the result is used as `s32 *` / `void *`).
- D_800A3708 (pointer to the 0x58-byte Unk80101DF0Record at 0x80101DF0, include/code6cac.h): code6cac_c2
  declared `Unk80101DF0Record *` and reads work.t[0] / work.t[2]; config declared `u8 *` and read the same two
  words as `*(s32 *)(D_800A3708 + 0x4C)` / `+ 0x54` (work at +0x38, t at +0x14 in it). config now includes
  code6cac.h, declares `extern Unk80101DF0Record *D_800A3708;` and reads `D_800A3708->work.t[0]` / `t[2]`,
  as code6cac_c2's func_8003E6D8 does.

Changed completed body (layer-2, keys: memory/grind/q65-adoption/q56/adopt/body_hashes.txt step06):
stage_InitCollision (config.c) - the two D_800A3708 reads above.
